{%- comment -%}
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  pf-swatch-main  —  product page for the FREE SWATCH BOOK
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  A deliberately separate section file, NOT a copy of pf-product-main.

  WHY A SEPARATE FILE AT ALL
    A template (templates/product.*.json) is only a list of which
    sections to render and what their settings are. It is not code.
    Two templates that both say "type": "pf-product-main" share ONE
    file — so editing that file changes the fabric pages too. The only
    way for this page to change on its own is for it to have its own
    section file. This is it.

  WHY THE CLASS PREFIX IS pfsw- AND NOT pf-
    Section {% stylesheet %} blocks are concatenated into one global
    stylesheet for the whole theme. A separate FILE is not a separate
    SCOPE: if this section reused .pf-pdp / .pf-price-line, its rules
    would still land on the fabric pages, and vice versa. Every
    selector below is prefixed pfsw- and appears nowhere else, so the
    two pages cannot reach each other.

  WHAT IT SHOWS
    Title, price, add-to-cart. Description underneath. Nothing else —
    no sq-ft calculator, no artwork upload, no size picker, because a
    free swatch book has no size and no artwork.
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign pfsw_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign pfsw_heading = section.settings.heading | default: product.title
  assign pfsw_button = section.settings.button_label | default: 'Add to cart'
-%}

<div class="pfsw" id="pfsw-{{ section.id }}">
  <div class="pfsw-top">
    {%- comment -%}
      EVERY image, not just the featured one. This started as a single
      product.featured_image, which quietly showed one photo however many
      were uploaded — a swatch book with a detail shot lost the detail
      shot. The hero swaps, the rail below selects.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if section.settings.show_image and product.images.size > 0 -%}
      {%- assign pfsw_hero = product.featured_image | default: product.images.first -%}
      <div class="pfsw-media">
        <img
          class="pfsw-media__main"
          data-pfsw-main
          src="{{ pfsw_hero | image_url: width: 800 }}"
          srcset="{{ pfsw_hero | image_url: width: 400 }} 400w,
                  {{ pfsw_hero | image_url: width: 600 }} 600w,
                  {{ pfsw_hero | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w,
                  {{ pfsw_hero | image_url: width: 1200 }} 1200w"
          sizes="(min-width: 1001px) 44vw, 92vw"
          width="{{ pfsw_hero.width }}"
          height="{{ pfsw_hero.height }}"
          alt="{{ pfsw_hero.alt | default: product.title | escape }}"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
          decoding="async"
        >

        {%- comment -%}
          Only when there is something to switch between — a one-image
          product gets no rail rather than a rail of one.

          Real <button>s, so they are tabbable and announce their pressed
          state. The active thumb is matched on image id rather than
          forloop.first: the featured image is normally the first, but
          matching on identity cannot be wrong if it ever is not.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if product.images.size > 1 -%}
          <div class="pfsw-thumbs" role="group" aria-label="{{ product.title | escape }} images">
            {%- for image in product.images -%}
              {%- assign pfsw_on = false -%}
              {%- if image.id == pfsw_hero.id -%}{%- assign pfsw_on = true -%}{%- endif -%}
              <button
                type="button"
                class="pfsw-thumb{% if pfsw_on %} is-on{% endif %}"
                data-pfsw-thumb
                data-full="{{ image | image_url: width: 800 }}"
                data-srcset="{{ image | image_url: width: 400 }} 400w, {{ image | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w, {{ image | image_url: width: 1200 }} 1200w"
                data-alt="{{ image.alt | default: product.title | escape }}"
                data-w="{{ image.width }}"
                data-h="{{ image.height }}"
                aria-pressed="{% if pfsw_on %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
              >
                <img
                  src="{{ image | image_url: width: 200 }}"
                  srcset="{{ image | image_url: width: 200 }} 200w, {{ image | image_url: width: 400 }} 400w"
                  sizes="84px"
                  width="{{ image.width }}"
                  height="{{ image.height }}"
                  alt="{{ product.title | escape }} — view {{ forloop.index }}"
                  loading="lazy"
                  decoding="async"
                >
              </button>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="pfsw-info">
      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <div class="pfsw-eyebrow">
          <span class="pfsw-cmyk" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
          {{ section.settings.eyebrow }}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <h1 class="pfsw-title">{{ pfsw_heading }}</h1>

      {%- comment -%}
        A swatch book is normally priced at 0, and "$0.00" reads like a
        bug rather than an offer. Anything above zero prints as money,
        so a paid book still works without touching this file.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="pfsw-price-line">
        {%- if pfsw_variant.price == 0 -%}
          <b class="pfsw-price pfsw-price--free">{{ section.settings.free_label | default: 'FREE' }}</b>
        {%- else -%}
          <b class="pfsw-price">{{ pfsw_variant.price | money }}</b>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.price_note != blank -%}
          <span class="pfsw-price-note">{{ section.settings.price_note }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        A real <form> posting to /cart/add, so the button works with JS
        off and with the cart set to a page instead of a drawer. The
        script at the bottom upgrades it to an in-place add.

        routes.cart_add_url rather than a hardcoded /cart/add: on a
        locale-prefixed storefront the hardcoded path drops the prefix
        and the add is rejected.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <form
        class="pfsw-form"
        method="post"
        action="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}"
        enctype="multipart/form-data"
        accept-charset="UTF-8"
        data-cart-url="{{ routes.cart_url }}"
      >
        <input type="hidden" name="form_type" value="product">
        <input type="hidden" name="utf8" value="✓">

        {%- if product.variants.size > 1 -%}
          <div class="pfsw-field">
            <label for="pfsw-variant-{{ section.id }}">{{ product.options.first | default: 'Option' }}</label>
            <select
              class="pfsw-variant-select"
              id="pfsw-variant-{{ section.id }}"
              name="id"
            >
              {%- for v in product.variants -%}
                <option
                  value="{{ v.id }}"
                  {% if v.id == pfsw_variant.id %}selected{% endif %}
                  {% unless v.available %}disabled{% endunless %}
                >
                  {{ v.title }}{% unless v.available %} — sold out{% endunless %}
                </option>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </select>
          </div>
        {%- else -%}
          <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ pfsw_variant.id }}">
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          One per customer is the whole point of a free sample, so the
          quantity is fixed rather than exposed as a stepper.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1">

        <button
          type="submit"
          name="add"
          class="pfsw-add"
          {% unless pfsw_variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %}
        >
          {%- if pfsw_variant.available -%}
            {{ pfsw_button }}
          {%- else -%}
            {{ section.settings.sold_out_label | default: 'Currently unavailable' }}
          {%- endif -%}
        </button>

        <p class="pfsw-msg" role="status" hidden></p>
      </form>

      {%- if section.settings.note != blank -%}
        <div class="pfsw-note">{{ section.settings.note }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.show_sku and pfsw_variant.sku != blank -%}
        <div class="pfsw-sku">SKU: <b>{{ pfsw_variant.sku }}</b></div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- if section.settings.show_description and product.description != blank -%}
    <div class="pfsw-desc">
      {%- if section.settings.description_heading != blank -%}
        <h2 class="pfsw-desc-heading">{{ section.settings.description_heading }}</h2>
      {%- endif -%}
      <div class="pfsw-desc-body rte">{{ product.description }}</div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

<script>
  (function () {
    'use strict';

    /* ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       WHY THE DRAWER ONCE SAID "YOUR CART IS EMPTY" AFTER A GOOD ADD

       The drawer's contents are rendered by the server when the page
       loads. Clicking the header's cart button only OPENS that dialog —
       it never goes and fetches the cart again. So adding through a
       plain POST to /cart/add.js put the item in the cart (the server
       was right all along) and then opened a panel whose HTML was still
       the one rendered before the add: the empty state. A reload showed
       the item, which is the tell.

       The theme's own buy buttons avoid this by asking Shopify to
       re-render the affected sections IN THE SAME request and swapping
       that HTML in. PFCart below does the same, in three tiers:

         1. /cart/add.js with `sections` → swap the returned HTML in.
         2. No section ids to ask for (some themes render the drawer in
            the layout) → re-fetch this page and lift the fresh
            #cart-drawer markup out of it.
         3. Both failed → go to the cart page, rather than open a panel
            that lies.

       The drawer is only opened once the swap has happened.
       ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

    if (!window.PFCart) {
      /* Defined defensively here AND in pf-swatch-cta.liquid, so neither
         file depends on the other being on the page. Whichever loads
         first wins — keep the two copies in step. */
      window.PFCart = (function () {
        var PREFIX = 'shopify-section-';

        function sectionIdOf(el) {
          if (!el || typeof el.closest !== 'function') return null;
          var wrap = el.closest('[id^="' + PREFIX + '"]');
          return wrap ? wrap.id.slice(PREFIX.length) : null;
        }

        /* The drawer, plus the header for the count bubble. Read from the
           DOM rather than hardcoded: a section inside a section group has
           a generated id like sections--1234__header. */
        function ids() {
          var out = [];
          var hosts = [
            document.getElementById('cart-drawer'),
            document.querySelector('cart-icon, [data-testid="cart-icon"]')
          ];
          hosts.forEach(function (el) {
            var id = sectionIdOf(el);
            if (id && out.indexOf(id) === -1) out.push(id);
          });
          return out;
        }

        /* Section Rendering API hands back whole sections, wrapper and
           all, so lift the inner HTML out and leave the live wrapper in
           place — replacing the wrapper itself would drop the id the
           theme uses to find it. */
        function apply(sections) {
          if (!sections) return false;
          var swapped = false;
          Object.keys(sections).forEach(function (id) {
            var host = document.getElementById(PREFIX + id);
            var html = sections[id];
            if (!host || !html) return;
            var doc = new DOMParser().parseFromString(html, 'text/html');
            var fresh = doc.getElementById(PREFIX + id) || doc.body;
            host.innerHTML = fresh.innerHTML;
            swapped = true;
          });
          return swapped;
        }

        function refetch() {
          return fetch(window.location.href, {
            credentials: 'same-origin',
            headers: { Accept: 'text/html' }
          })
            .then(function (response) {
              if (!response.ok) throw new Error('page fetch ' + response.status);
              return response.text();
            })
            .then(function (html) {
              var doc = new DOMParser().parseFromString(html, 'text/html');
              var swapped = false;
              ['#cart-drawer', 'cart-icon'].forEach(function (selector) {
                var live = document.querySelector(selector);
                var fresh = doc.querySelector(selector);
                if (!live || !fresh) return;
                live.innerHTML = fresh.innerHTML;
                swapped = true;
              });
              return swapped;
            })
            .catch(function () {
              return false;
            });
        }

        function open(cartUrl) {
          var trigger = document.querySelector(
            '[data-testid="cart-drawer-trigger"], [aria-controls="cart-drawer"]'
          );
          if (trigger) {
            trigger.click();
            return true;
          }
          /* Cart type is "page", not "drawer". */
          window.location.href = cartUrl || '/cart';
          return false;
        }

        /* Resolves true when the drawer is open on fresh contents, false
           when it gave up and navigated. Rejects only if the add itself
           was refused. */
        function add(variantId, quantity, addUrl, cartUrl) {
          var wanted = ids();
          var body = {
            items: [{ id: Number(variantId), quantity: quantity || 1 }],
            sections_url: window.location.pathname + window.location.search
          };
          if (wanted.length) body.sections = wanted.join(',');

          return fetch(addUrl || '/cart/add.js', {
            method: 'POST',
            credentials: 'same-origin',
            headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', Accept: 'application/json' },
            body: JSON.stringify(body)
          })
            .then(function (response) {
              if (!response.ok) throw new Error('add failed: ' + response.status);
              return response.json();
            })
            .then(function (data) {
              if (apply(data && data.sections)) return true;
              return refetch();
            })
            .then(function (swapped) {
              if (!swapped) {
                window.location.href = cartUrl || '/cart';
                return false;
              }
              return open(cartUrl);
            });
        }

        return { add: add, ids: ids, apply: apply, refetch: refetch, open: open };
      })();
    }

    /* Delegated from document, so nothing here holds a reference that
       could go stale when the theme editor re-renders the section — or
       when PFCart swaps the header out from under it. */
    if (window.__pfSwatchMain) return;
    window.__pfSwatchMain = true;
    /* ── Thumbnail rail ──────────────────────────────────────────
       Delegated from document, so it holds no element reference to go
       stale when the theme editor re-renders the section.

       width/height are swapped along with the src. Those attributes give
       the browser an aspect ratio to reserve before the image loads, and
       leaving them on the previous image's numbers would letterbox or
       stretch a photo of a different shape. ─────────────────────── */
    document.addEventListener('click', function (event) {
      var thumb = event.target && event.target.closest
        ? event.target.closest('[data-pfsw-thumb]')
        : null;
      if (!thumb) return;

      var media = thumb.closest('.pfsw-media');
      var main = media && media.querySelector('[data-pfsw-main]');
      if (!main) return;

      var full = thumb.getAttribute('data-full');
      if (!full) return;

      main.src = full;
      main.srcset = thumb.getAttribute('data-srcset') || '';
      main.alt = thumb.getAttribute('data-alt') || main.alt;

      var w = thumb.getAttribute('data-w');
      var h = thumb.getAttribute('data-h');
      if (w && h) {
        main.setAttribute('width', w);
        main.setAttribute('height', h);
      }

      Array.prototype.forEach.call(media.querySelectorAll('[data-pfsw-thumb]'), function (el) {
        var on = el === thumb;
        el.classList.toggle('is-on', on);
        el.setAttribute('aria-pressed', on ? 'true' : 'false');
      });
    });

    function say(form, text, bad) {
      var msg = form.querySelector('.pfsw-msg');
      if (!msg) return;
      msg.textContent = text || '';
      msg.hidden = !text;
      msg.classList.toggle('pfsw-msg--bad', !!bad);
    }

    document.addEventListener('submit', function (event) {
      var form = event.target;
      if (!form || typeof form.matches !== 'function' || !form.matches('.pfsw-form')) return;

      /* No fetch or no DOMParser (very old browser, blocked request) —
         let the plain POST happen exactly as it would have. */
      if (typeof window.fetch !== 'function' || typeof window.DOMParser !== 'function') return;

      event.preventDefault();

      var button = form.querySelector('.pfsw-add');
      if (!button || button.getAttribute('data-pf-busy')) return;

      var idField = form.querySelector('[name="id"]');
      var id = idField && idField.value;
      if (!id) {
        form.submit();
        return;
      }

      var label = button.textContent.trim();
      var cartUrl = form.getAttribute('data-cart-url') || '/cart';

      button.setAttribute('data-pf-busy', '1');
      button.textContent = 'Adding…';
      say(form, '');

      window.PFCart.add(id, 1, form.getAttribute('action') + '.js', cartUrl)
        .then(function (opened) {
          /* Navigating away — leave the button as it is rather than
             flicker back to its label on the way out. */
          if (!opened) return;
          button.textContent = 'Added ✓';
          window.setTimeout(function () {
            button.textContent = label;
            button.removeAttribute('data-pf-busy');
          }, 2000);
        })
        .catch(function () {
          button.textContent = label;
          button.removeAttribute('data-pf-busy');
          say(form, 'Sorry — we could not add that just now. Please try again.', true);
        });
    });
  })();
</script>

{% stylesheet %}
  /* ═══ Free swatch book page. Every selector is pfsw- prefixed and
     used nowhere else in the theme — see the note at the top of the
     file for why that matters. ═══ */
  .pfsw {
    --pfsw-magenta: #e20a6e;
    --pfsw-ink: #141c33;
    --pfsw-muted: #7a7f8e;
    --pfsw-line: #dad5cb;

    max-width: 1180px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: clamp(20px, 4vw, 44px) clamp(16px, 4vw, 32px) clamp(32px, 6vw, 64px);
    color: var(--pfsw-ink);
  }

  .pfsw-top {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: clamp(20px, 4vw, 48px);
    align-items: start;
  }

  /* One column when there is no image, so the text does not sit in a
     half-width column with nothing beside it. */
  .pfsw-top:not(:has(.pfsw-media)) {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 640px);
  }

  /* Scoped to the hero, not .pfsw-media img — the thumbnails live in the
     same wrapper and must not inherit the 14px hero radius. */
  .pfsw-media__main {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: #f4f2ee;
  }

  .pfsw-thumbs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-top: 12px;
  }

  .pfsw-thumb {
    width: 84px;
    padding: 0;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--pfsw-line);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: #f4f2ee;
    overflow: hidden;
    /* line-height:0 or the button keeps a text baseline gap under the img */
    line-height: 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    appearance: none;
    -webkit-appearance: none;
    transition: border-color 0.18s ease;
  }

  .pfsw-thumb img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .pfsw-thumb:hover {
    border-color: var(--pfsw-muted);
  }

  .pfsw-thumb.is-on {
    border-color: var(--pfsw-magenta);
  }

  .pfsw-thumb:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--pfsw-magenta) !important;
    outline-offset: 2px !important;
  }

  .pfsw-info {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .pfsw-eyebrow {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--pfsw-muted);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .pfsw-cmyk {
    display: inline-flex;
    gap: 3px;
  }

  .pfsw-cmyk i {
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    border-radius: 50%;
  }

  .pfsw-cmyk i:nth-child(1) { background: #00b3e3; }
  .pfsw-cmyk i:nth-child(2) { background: #e20a6e; }
  .pfsw-cmyk i:nth-child(3) { background: #f0b408; }
  .pfsw-cmyk i:nth-child(4) { background: #141c33; }

  .pfsw-title {
    font-size: clamp(26px, 4.6vw, 38px);
    font-weight: 900;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--pfsw-ink);
  }

  .pfsw-price-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .pfsw-price {
    font-size: clamp(24px, 4vw, 30px);
    font-weight: 900;
    color: var(--pfsw-ink);
  }

  .pfsw-price--free {
    color: var(--pfsw-magenta);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .pfsw-price-note {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--pfsw-muted);
  }

  .pfsw-form {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    max-width: 420px;
  }

  .pfsw-field {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 5px;
  }

  .pfsw-field label {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .pfsw-variant-select {
    font: inherit;
    padding: 10px 12px;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--pfsw-line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    width: 100%;
    background: #fff;
  }

  .pfsw-variant-select:focus {
    outline: none;
    border-color: var(--pfsw-magenta);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(226, 10, 110, 0.12);
  }

  .pfsw-add {
    min-height: var(--minimum-touch-target, 48px);
    background: var(--pfsw-magenta);
    color: #fff;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1rem;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 14px 20px;
    cursor: pointer;
    appearance: none;
    -webkit-appearance: none;
    transition: background 0.18s ease;
  }

  .pfsw-add:hover:not([disabled]) {
    background: #c1085d;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .pfsw-add[disabled] {
    background: var(--pfsw-line);
    color: #6b6b6b;
    cursor: not-allowed;
  }

  .pfsw-add:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--pfsw-ink) !important;
    outline-offset: 2px !important;
  }

  .pfsw-msg {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .pfsw-msg[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .pfsw-msg--bad {
    color: #c1085d;
  }

  .pfsw-note {
    margin-top: 16px;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--pfsw-muted);
  }

  .pfsw-note p {
    margin: 0 0 6px;
  }

  .pfsw-sku {
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--pfsw-muted);
  }

  .pfsw-desc {
    margin-top: clamp(28px, 5vw, 56px);
    padding-top: clamp(20px, 3vw, 32px);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--pfsw-line);
    max-width: 820px;
  }

  .pfsw-desc-heading {
    font-size: clamp(18px, 2.6vw, 22px);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }

  .pfsw-desc-body {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #3c4258;
  }

  .pfsw-desc-body img {
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .pfsw-desc-body table {
    width: 100%;
    overflow-x: auto;
    display: block;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .pfsw-top {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .pfsw-form {
      max-width: none;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "PF Swatch main",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "pfsw-section-wrapper",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "FREE SWATCH BOOK" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading (blank = product title)" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_image", "label": "Show product images", "default": true },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Price" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "free_label", "label": "Label when the price is 0", "default": "FREE" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "price_note", "label": "Price note", "default": "delivered free · one per customer" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Add to cart" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "button_label", "label": "Button label", "default": "Add to cart" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "sold_out_label", "label": "Sold-out label", "default": "Currently unavailable" },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "note", "label": "Note under the button", "default": "<p>Ships within 1 business day. Swatches are cut from the same rolls we print your order on.</p>" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_sku", "label": "Show SKU", "default": false },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Description" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_description", "label": "Show product description below", "default": true },
    { "type": "text", "id": "description_heading", "label": "Description heading (optional)" }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "PF Swatch main" }]
}
{% endschema %}
